EXPERIMENT 23 – BLACK-BOX TESTING ON LOGIN MODULE
AIM
To execute black-box testing on a login module by checking its behaviour against the specification without knowing its internal code or structure.
ALGORITHM
1. Study the login module specification without looking at its code.
2. Design test cases for valid data, invalid data, blank fields, special characters, case sensitivity and account locking.
3. Execute every test case using the given test data.
4. Compare actual results with expected results and record Pass or Fail.
5. Prepare a decision table for login rules and add test cases for blank fields, length limits and security.
6. Reset the account before tests involving wrong attempts.
7. Report failed test cases as defects.
INPUT
Login specifications:
- Username: 6–20 letters or digits.
- Password: 8–16 characters with one capital letter, one digit and one special character.
- Account locked after 3 wrong attempts.
- Test account: student / Secret@123
Decision Table
Condition / Action	R1	R2	R3	R4
Valid username	Yes	Yes	No	No
Valid password	Yes	No	Yes	No
Action	Home page	Error message	Error message	Error message

Test Cases
TC ID	Test Scenario	Test Data	Expected Result	Status
TC01	Valid username and password	student / Secret@123	Home page displayed	Pass
TC02	Wrong password	student / wrong	Invalid credentials	Pass
TC03	Wrong username	stud / Secret@123	Invalid credentials	Pass
TC04	Both fields blank	Blank / Blank	Both fields required	Pass
TC05	Username blank	Blank / Secret@123	Username required	Pass
TC06	Password blank	student / Blank	Password required	Pass
TC07	Case-sensitive password	student / secret@123	Invalid credentials	Pass
TC08	SQL injection	' OR '1'='1 / abc	Login rejected	Pass
TC09	Password masking	Any password	Characters shown as dots	Pass
TC10	Account lock	3 wrong attempts	Account locked	Pass
TC11	Back button after logout	Login, logout, press Back	Login page displayed; session not reused	Pass
TC12	Spaces around username	student / Secret@123	Login accepted after trimming spaces	Pass

OUTPUT
